1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:07,450
A sales call is starting. Lynkk noticed it, and one click starts

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:14,650
the recording. Look at the call: two people, and nothing else joined.

3
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:21,070
After every sales call there are the same four jobs. Write up

4
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:26,890
the notes. Pull out the next steps. Send the recap. Book the

5
00:00:26,940 --> 00:00:32,710
next meeting. Then the next call starts, and the details from this

6
00:00:32,760 --> 00:00:34,650
one start to fade.

7
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:41,598
Lynkk covers the whole call: a briefing before it, notes while you

8
00:00:41,648 --> 00:00:47,947
talk, and a Meeting Brief with decisions and tasks after it. Here's

9
00:00:47,997 --> 00:00:51,650
a pilot-planning call from start to finish.

10
00:00:52,300 --> 00:01:02,392
With Google Calendar connected, Lynkk sends a morning briefing on days you

11
00:01:02,442 --> 00:01:12,534
have meetings. For each one: who you're meeting, your last note with

12
00:01:12,584 --> 00:01:21,831
them, and how many action items are still open between you.

13
00:01:21,881 --> 00:01:31,973
With Ask Lynkk, on Pro, you can ask your own notes a

14
00:01:32,023 --> 00:01:42,115
question. The answer shows its sources, and one click plays the moment

15
00:01:42,165 --> 00:01:44,650
it was said.

16
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:52,140
MAYA: Is it alright if I record this so I don't have to

17
00:01:52,190 --> 00:01:53,288
MAYA: take notes?

18
00:01:53,338 --> 00:01:53,862
DANIEL: Sure.

19
00:01:53,912 --> 00:02:00,752
On the Mac, Lynkk records both sides of the call on two

20
00:02:00,802 --> 00:02:07,642
channels, so your side of the transcript is labelled 'You'. No bot

21
00:02:07,692 --> 00:02:08,216
joins.

22
00:02:08,266 --> 00:02:15,106
The live words sit on the edge of your screen, and you

23
00:02:15,156 --> 00:02:19,699
